from http.server import SimpleHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer
from urllib.parse import urlparse, parse_qs
queues, results, lock = {}, {}, threading.Lock()
log = open('log.jsonl', 'a', buffering=1)
class H(SimpleHTTPRequestHandler):
    def log_message(self, *a): pass
    def _json(self, v):
        b = json.dumps(v).encode(); self.send_response(200)
        self.send_header('Content-Type','application/json'); self.send_header('Access-Control-Allow-Origin','*'); self.end_headers(); self.wfile.write(b)
    def end_headers(self):
        self.send_header('Cache-Control','no-store'); super().end_headers()
    def do_GET(self):
        u = urlparse(self.path); q = parse_qs(u.query)
        if u.path == '/cmd':
            with lock: items = queues.pop(q.get('panel',[''])[0], [])
            return self._json(items)
